  "worked_solution": "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+20\\lambda +100 & =0 \\\\ {(\\lambda +10)}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have a repeated root $\\lambda =-10,$ so we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-10x}+Bx{e}^{-10x}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=5$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA=5.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=-5,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=-10A{e}^{-10x}+B{e}^{-10x}-10Bx{e}^{-10x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=-5$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-10A+B=-5.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $A=5$ gives $B=45.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=5{e}^{-10x}+45x{e}^{-10x}.\n$$",
